<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much should a Dubai salon spend on marketing per month?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most independent salons in Dubai see solid results starting between AED 3,000–8,000/month once the free channels (Google Business Profile, reviews, booking flow) are already in shape."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What's the fastest way to get more bookings without spending on ads?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Fixing your Google Business Profile and review response speed. Both are free, and for most salons they're the single highest-ROI channel."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I run Instagram ads or Google Ads first?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If your booking flow and Google Maps presence are already solid, Google Ads usually wins first because it captures people who are actively searching and ready to book. Instagram is better for building longer-term demand and brand recognition."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to see results from salon SEO?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Typically 2–4 months for meaningful movement in Google Maps rankings and organic traffic, though a well-optimised Google Business Profile can lift map visibility within weeks."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a marketing agency, or can I do this myself?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Everything in this guide is doable in-house if you have the time and consistency. Most owners outsource it because running a salon and running a marketing system at the same time is two full-time jobs."}}]}</script>

			
			
